flowchart TB
    accTitle: Which folder names an installation uses
    accDescr: For each folder name and fallback name, an installation uses the name that its settings saved, whatever the language. An installation that an earlier version set up, with a target user or with copies and imports of its runs, keeps the German name of those versions, such as Archiv, for a name that it never saved. An installation in use on a French or Spanish Nextcloud keeps the English name that it has from the versions before these languages. A new installation proposes the name in the default language of Nextcloud when the app has a catalog for that language or for its generic one, such as German for de_DE, and in English otherwise, such as Archive. Saving the settings keeps the names that the page shows, and the first run stores a name that it uses, so that no other language renames the folder afterwards. The questions are indigo and the names in Nextcloud blue.

    name["A folder name or<br>a fallback name"] --> saved{"Saved in<br>the settings?"}
    saved -->|yes| keep["The saved name"]
    saved -->|no| earlier{"Set up by an<br>earlier version, with a<br>target user or a run?"}
    earlier -->|yes| german["The German name of<br>the earlier versions,<br>such as Archiv"]
    earlier -->|no| inuse{"In use on a French or<br>Spanish Nextcloud before<br>these languages came?"}
    inuse -->|yes| kept["The English name that<br>it has, such as Archive"]
    inuse -->|no| language{"A catalog for the<br>default language of<br>Nextcloud, or for its<br>generic one?"}
    language -->|yes| localized["The name in that<br>language, such as<br>Archiv for de or de_DE"]
    language -->|no| english["The English name,<br>such as Archive"]
    localized --> stored["The first run stores the<br>name that it uses, so no<br>other language renames it"]
    english --> stored

    classDef check fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef nextcloud fill:#0082c92e,stroke:#0082c9,stroke-width:2px
    class saved,earlier,inuse,language check
    class keep,german,kept,localized,english,stored nextcloud
